{
  "_meta": {
    "title": "Replace person in video, masked mannequin mode (MiniMax H3)",
    "description": "SAM 3.1 tracks the person; inside a 40 px edit mask the person becomes a smooth grey mannequin in the motion reference (pose kept, identity/clothes hidden; idea from openjutsu, MIT), H3 Ref2VA renders <Picture 1> into the mask only (H3RelayApplyEditMask), CJPasteBackSave pastes the masked pixels back at source resolution with the source audio. Motion guide (default Pose): RT-DETR + SDPose whole-body keypoints are read from the source with everything outside the edit mask blacked out (one person, the tracked subject), the drawn skeleton is re-masked to the edit area and drives MiniMaxH3FunControlNetApply (Fun ControlNet Union 2.0) on the sampling model; the builder removes nodes 60-70 when the guide is Off. 2K finish (Finish picker, default Off; nodes 80-95, Open-H3-Regenerate node pack + core MiniMaxH3LatentUpscaleWithModel): the trimmed swap frames are prepared at 576p, encoded, upscaled in latent space to the 1080p grid (H3 latent upscaler), re-rendered with the Open-H3-Regenerate 2K LoRA + sharp curve in 3 euler steps from start_sigma (default 0.5) under the same Ref2VA conditioning and noise, cropped 1088 -> 1080, aligned back to the swap frames' aspect (CJRegenAlign) and fed to CJPasteBackSave with output_res 'frames' (source upscaled to the finish's size). Shipped detached; the builder removes 80-95 when Finish is Off and wires them in for 2K."
  },
